  "details": "I'm not sure how common that is, but I found that bug in a party world when was trying to do some pool Photos(tried in a few other worlds, but didn't find similar situations) .\nWhat this bug does is when you stay in a water, bring a camera out and press Semi-auto in a focus section, it just starts rendering what camera \"sees\" in a very wierd way, you can almost literally see the borders of a geometric figure, including that those borders change when you change \"zoom\" setting, and worst part - whole picture \"insinde\" of said area(geometric figure) starts rendering differently in different Eyes(excluding when you hold camera straight horizontally). It stops doing so only when you turn off camera, and bug continue appear every time you pull out camera afterwards, even without pressing Focus.\nSome screenshots of a bug:\n1.Water without camera out\n2.Water right after pulling camera out with focusing\n3.Water when I lift camera sideways, difference in eyes especially visible on a left side\n4.Worst case - when I turn around camera to make selfie(or press \"Track self\"), difference in Eyes is extreme\nHow to repeat:\n1.Go to this world https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_860bdea8-0499-4c16-8170-5683a3a3ab8a\n2.Find a pool(turn right after spawning in a world and find stair on a second floor), stand in a middle of waterpool\n3.Pull out Camera, go to Focus and turn on Semi Auto",
